From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:50:07 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] wordcraft-web: add an opt-in postMessage host bridge
 (?host=parent)

A page that frames WordCraft in an <iframe> can now open a document in it,
ask it to save, and hear about unsaved changes, the way the GridCraft and
PDFCraft web apps already allow for their embedders.

Messages are plain objects with a `type`:
  wordcraft:ready       (to host)   {version}
  wordcraft:open        (from host) {name, bytes}
  wordcraft:opened      (to host)   {name}
  wordcraft:requestSave (from host)
  wordcraft:save        (to host)   {name, bytes}, bytes transferred
  wordcraft:dirty       (to host)   {dirty}
  wordcraft:failed      (to host)   {error}

Only the parent window is heard or answered, and only on its origin: the
page's own, or the one named by &parent_origin=. Without ?host=parent, or
without a parent, nothing changes. In host mode the page starts with an
empty document instead of File > Home.
